\image(figures/xception_training.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Primary cross entropy from the visible Adam loop. Training uses augmentation and batch moments; validation is deterministic. Selection uses the unaugmented validation split.)
\alttext(Primary cross entropy from the visible Adam loop. Training uses augmentation and batch moments; validation is deterministic. Selection uses the unaugmented validation split.)

Training NLL uses minibatch moments and randomly transformed inputs. The selected
checkpoint uses saved population moments and original images when reporting
fitting, validation and test NLL.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/xception_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


